{"title":"2022 SSMO Tiebreaker Round Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of the 5 smallest positive prime numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b6e76dc8ae0d490db7c405e6b5b5f6d3b70c9aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^n+4^n\\equiv0 \\pmod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> has no positive integer solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that there are no solutions when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd70692c242910d2ed6a7fd7630cee3e320c6967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />. Assume otherwise. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/5495445984d1f764f4f523a4afd30d65649e4ce9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^n+4^n\\equiv0\\implies 3^n=-4^n\\implies\\left(3\\cdot4^{-1}\\right)^n\\equiv-1\\pmod{p}.\\]\" width=\"472\" height=\"21\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314204a0e28831367115862706c752154eb941db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3\\cdot4^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />. From Fermat's Little Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5c64cd5b1b6b01b6061b7388e50960d39aefea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{p-1}\\equiv1\\pmod{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"21\" />. The equation has no solutions if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a5387edbb19b6135671d6b252bf9eae39ea69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{d}\\equiv1\\pmod{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"22\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea01211c90eea50e9ac03e29843d33bf75298da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{p-1}{2^{v_2(p-1)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" /> is the largest odd integer dividing into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab0727c08c4aaa6fa119bd3fafe17851e431fd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />. Consider the following table \n\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\np &amp; a=3\\cdot 4^{-1}\\pmod{p} &amp; d=\\frac{p-1}{2^{v_2(p-1)}} &amp; a^d\\pmod{p} \\\\\n\\hline\n5 &amp; 2 &amp; 1 &amp; 2^1\\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\\\\n7 &amp; 6 &amp; 3 &amp; 6^3\\equiv 6 \\pmod{7} \\\\\n11 &amp; 9 &amp; 5 &amp; 9^5\\equiv 1 \\pmod{11} \\\\\n13 &amp; 4 &amp; 3 &amp; 4^3\\equiv 12 \\pmod{13} \\\\\n17 &amp; 5 &amp; 1 &amp; 5^1\\equiv 5 \\pmod{17} \\\\\n19 &amp; 15 &amp; 9 &amp; 15^9\\equiv 18 \\pmod{19} \\\\\n23 &amp; 18 &amp; 11 &amp; 18^{11}\\equiv 1 \\pmod{23} \\\\\n29 &amp; 8 &amp; 7 &amp; 8^7\\equiv 17 \\pmod{29} \\\\\n31 &amp; 24 &amp; 15 &amp; 24^{15}\\equiv 30 \\pmod{31} \\\\\n37 &amp; 10 &amp; 9 &amp; 10^9\\equiv 1 \\pmod{37}\n\\end{array}\\]\nSo, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b576f546862473483960a990d799ea62d03c9287.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2+3+11+23+37=\\boxed{76}.\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 44/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2057/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24672:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022314 and revision id 280217. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}